{
	"name": "Kidney Strike",
	"type": "maneuver",
	"img": "icons/weapons/daggers/knife-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Most people are delightfully unaware of just how many nerves they possess within their internal organs, but you’re adept at teaching them. As part of the attack action, you may force your opponent to make a Constitution saving throw or have their movement speed reduced to 0 by the sudden and crippling pain of your strike. The target also gains disadvantage on saving throws to avoid becoming stunned or confused. This effect ends at the start of your next turn.</p>",
